{"parentUuid":"c85546a9-5ad1-49db-afef-4b627faf0026","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdBhoYyWX2Z3EDBCBpEJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Opus: baseline vs +graph (15 tasks from official 300, 13 evaluated)\n\n| | baseline (no graph) | +graph | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **accuracy** | 11/13 = **85%** | 10/13 = **77%** | **−1** (noise) |\n| **tokens (real)** | 678,762 | 642,126 | **−5.4%** |\n| **$cost** | — | — | **−6.2%** |\n\n**Accuracy: graph ≈ 0** (−1 = one regression, rubocop; zero graph-only wins). Same as haiku — the graph doesn't add accuracy, even for a strong coder.\n\n**Tokens: graph saves −5.4% real / −6.2% cost.** Smaller than haiku-naive's −23% because opus navigates efficiently in smart mode (less reading to avoid), but still a real save.\n\n**The consistent finding, now confirmed on both models:** the graph is a **token/navigation win, accuracy-neutral.** Opus baseline is already 85% (clears its published 84.4% and Sonnet 5's 78.3% on this sample) — it's a strong coder on its own; the graph makes it ~5-6% cheaper at the same accuracy.\n\n(2 tasks — redis, tokio — never evaluated: docker images won't build locally. 13/13 is the clean common set.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":707951,"output_tokens":1319,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":707951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdBhoT1b5LdNSmbsFkA2g","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c1fffa7-1a66-4367-ab0