{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-07-31T02:59:46.248Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wv6ffuftd</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501/tasks/wv6ffuftd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Read every open front of entireio/entire-brain in parallel and synthesize a current-state briefing\" completed</summary>\n<result>\"# entire-brain — where we are (as of 2026-07-30)\\n\\n**Headline:** main has been quiet for 16 days (nothing merged since 2026-07-14; last commit `afe7d3f2` 2026-07-19). Three PRs are open, all untouched ≥12 days, all with **zero reviews and zero comments**. Nothing is blocked on other people — it is blocked on you.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. State of main\\n\\n- **Main tip** `afe7d3f2` (2026-07-19) \\\"Rename brain-bench to GraphMark\\\" — docs-only, 1 file (`docs/ga-readiness.md`), +6/−6. Parent `bc0203b7` = merge of PR #72 `chore/rename-entire-graph`.\\n- **Last real code merges were 07-12 → 07-14** (7 PRs): #72 Entire Graph adoption across Brain (+536/−451, 50 files), #71 Phase 0B temporal-memory causal harness (+9,299), #66 temporal-memory ablation benchmark (+5,726), #68 fact vitality serve receipts (+2,185), #67 adaptive project-memory retrieval (+3,034), #69 pending fact reviews in recall/brief, #65 camelCase fact-set wire fields. **Nothing merged since 07-14.**\\n- **Direction 1 — prove memory causally helps.** #71+#66 are ~15K added lines of preregistered ablation + causal harness; commit `f059ae0c` = \\\"valid harness-lane result — memory HELPS\\\". The lab is now the product.\\n- **Direction 2 — facts became a trust surface.** #68 vitality receipts + #69 pending-review surfacing mean facts now carry provenance/staleness/review state at serve time.\\n- **Direction 3 — naming/dependency consolidation onto Entire Graph.** #56 (sem → entireio/entire-sem) → #72 (Graph across Brain) → `afe7d3f2` (brain-bench → GraphMark). **GraphMark is external only:** `git grep entirehq/graphmark` on main = zero hits, no submodule, no CI job. The only coupling is prose in `docs/ga-readiness.md`. Note the name collision: in-repo `scripts/bench` (`\\\"entire-brain-bench\\\"`) is the *embedder* bench (Model2Vec vs EmbeddingGemma), not GraphMark; the real regression harness is `benchmarks/agent-brain/`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Open PRs\\n\\n### PR #73 — \\\"P0.M5: standalone install docs + announcement polish\\\"\\n- **Branch** `docs/p0m5-install-docs` → `main`, commit `073ea21`, created 2026-07-17, untouched since (~13d).\\n- **What:** docs-only, 2 files, +372/−104. `docs/getting-started.md` +246/−8 (553-byte stub → full cold-start install + first-run guide, grounded against the CLI, uses post-rename `entire graph`); `docs/release_press_release.md` +126/−96 (accuracy pass vs shipped v0.1.0, cites 28/30 languages p&lt;0.05, 1148 vs 802). No code.\\n- **Review/CI:** 0 reviews, 0 comments, 0 requested reviewers. CI **14/14 SUCCESS**, 1 skipped (`release-evidence`), run 29600651657. `mergeable=MERGEABLE`, `mergeStateStatus=CLEAN`.\\n- **Blocker:** none mechanical. Three author-flagged *publish* caveats (not merge gates): brain module path is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` not `entireio` so `go install github.com/entireio/entire-brain/...@v0.1.0` won't resolve (guide falls back to source install); `entire plugin install` doesn't resolve `requires: sem`, so provider install stays manual; need to confirm the v0.1.0 archive ships an `entire graph`-answering provider.\\n- **Next:** merge it (needs your approval). Docs-only, green, clean.\\n\\n### PR #74 — \\\"feat(facts): local git-meta-backed fact store + `facts sync`\\\"\\n- **Branch** `feat/facts-gitmeta-local` @ `bdd7ee33`, 3 commits, created 2026-07-17, +2,668/−11 across 17 files.\\n- **What:** implements the pre-existing `factsync.Server` seam with a fully local on-disk git-meta backend — no entiredb/Postgres/mTLS/network. `internal/factgitmeta/localrepo.go` (bare go-git v6 filesystem repo at 0o700 + flock); `internal/factgitmeta/backend.go` (records on git-meta `project` target, ref `refs/meta/local/main`; head key `brain:facts:&lt;hex(repoKey)&gt;:&lt;hex(branch)&gt;:head`, value `&lt;version&gt;|&lt;contentRef&gt;`, `OpCompareAndSet`; `contentRef = facts-&lt;sha256(plaintext)&gt;` — byte-identical to the hosted store); `internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/` vendors the git-meta engine verbatim from git-meta-service (Go can't import another module's `internal/`), with round-trip + golden byte-compat tests; `internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go` adds `facts sync` with `--facts-backend=local-gitmeta|http` (default local, env `ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BACKEND`), `http` fails closed behind `ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED=1`. Adds go-git v6 alpha, go-billy v6 alpha, termenv; bumps x/sys 0.42→0.45.\\n- **Review/CI:** 0 reviews, 0 comments. `mergeable=MERGEABLE`, `mergeStateStatus=UNSTABLE` — **CI red** (run 29616985234).\\n- **Blockers (all yours, all mechanical):**\\n  1. **Windows build break** — `syscall.Flock`/`LOCK_EX` are unix-only; kills `build (windows,amd64)`, `test (windows-latest)`, `phase1-semantic (windows-latest)`. Code comment assumes \\\"unix dev-machine tool\\\"; CI disagrees.\\n  2. **gofmt** — `internal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go` unformatted (two one-line goroutine bodies ~line 284); still unformatted in the working tree today.\\n  3. **PR body stale** — documents blob key as `...:blob:&lt;contentRef&gt;`; `bdd7ee33` changed it to a single per-branch `:blob` key.\\n  4. Author's own gate: body says \\\"Do not merge — for review\\\". Shared publication (pushing to `refs/meta/*` in entiredb) is deliberately out of scope, still blocked on the **entiredb reserved-ref unblock**.\\n- **Next:** split flock into `lock_unix.go` (`//go:build !windows`) + `lock_windows.go` (`LockFileEx` via `golang.org/x/sys/windows`, already a direct dep); `gofmt -w internal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go`; fix the blob-key paragraph; push, get green, request review. **Do not carry `d0ba1e06` (init-agents) onto this branch** — the local checkout sits one commit past the PR head.\\n\\n### PR #75 — \\\"Improve Brain brief retrieval and harden its evaluation pipeline\\\" (DRAFT)\\n- **Branch** `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` @ `923b8a91`, author `ashtom`, created 2026-07-18, untouched since. **552 files, 120 commits, +199,356/−556.** (`gh pr diff` returns HTTP 406 — GitHub can't render it; `gh pr view` truncates files/commits at 100, and per-file stats read 0/0 for ~150 files. Body's \\\"116 ahead / 83 behind\\\" is stale; actual **120 ahead / 84 behind**.)\\n- **Split:** `benchmarks/agent-brain/**` = 477 files / +182,008 (confirmatory 185, mined-scale 147, mined-c0701 94, analysis 21). Product code = 30 non-test Go files in `internal/cli` (+6,548/−343) + 39 test files (+10,412).\\n- **What (product):** new `brain_brief_compact{,_v2,_v3}.go`, `brain_brief_git_intent.go`, `brain_brief_action_relevance.go`, `brain_brief_stale_index.go`, `brain_brief_semantic_{dedupe,freshness}.go`, `semantic_test_suggestions.go`, `facts_eligibility.go`, `history_legacy_identity.go`; big edits to `agent_surface.go` (+995), `history_fts.go`, `history.go`. MCP `brain_brief` gains `packet_format` enum `legacy_json|compact_v1|compact_v2|compact_v3`; **default stays `legacy_json`** → zero default-behavior change.\\n- **What (eval):** fail-closed contracts + verifiers — temporal eligibility, treatment isolation (`no_memory`/`placebo_packet`/`retrieved_memory`/`oracle_retrieval`), task-validity lint + review ledger, Latin-square scheduling with resume, engine identity, 7 negative controls, content-addressed evidence, `confirmatory/check_protocol.py` (4,118 lines), `run.py` +2,785.\\n- **Claimed measurements** (author's, scenario-specific, \\\"not additive\\\"): legacy history ranking 471 ms → 117 ms (−75.2%), allocated bytes −99.93%; duplicate semantic roots −13.73% o200k tokens; action-relevance gate false actions 11 → 0, JSON 14,097 → 10,742 B (−23.80%); Git-intent overlay all 4 targets to edit-rank #1; test-suggestion Hit@8 0/8 → 6/8. **Reproducibility gap admitted:** the Hit@8 headline is not re-derivable (no-write replay can't open the SQLite stores, judgment map never persisted).\\n- **Review/CI:** 0 reviews, 0 comments. Only check = Cursor Bugbot SUCCESS, \\\"Medium Risk\\\". `mergeable=false` / `dirty`.\\n- **Blocker:** **11 real content conflicts** (`git merge-tree` exit 1): `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py`, `run_test.py`, `docs/getting-started.md`, `internal\n... (truncated 13342 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501/tasks/wv6ffuftd.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/subagents/workflows/wf_e29d9e34-272/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/workflows/scripts/entire-brain-state-audit-wf_e29d9e34-272.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_e29d9e34-272'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>9</agent_count><agents_done>9</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>519896</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>108</tool_uses><duration_ms>336084</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
