vault symlinked + entire brain MCP wired in devenv; distill after sessions end\n9\t- [Devenv codebase map](devenv-codebase-map.md) — full Entire-suite architecture map at devenv/CODEBASE-MAP.md (CLAUDE.md @-ref); don't re-discover, update it\n10\t- [Cost analytics state](cost-analytics-state.md) — round 2 done 2026-07-10: cli #1702 + entire-api #261 + web branch staged (PR user-gated); never merge to main without approval\n11\t- [Orchestrator architecture](orchestrator-architecture.md) — standing mode 2026-07-11: Fable orchestrates only, opus/sonnet tiers, live-verification doctrine, mutation-verified tests, NO AI commit footers, 10-min review sweeps\n12\t- [CLI bug-batch PRs](cli-bug-batch-prs.md) — 8 live-repro'd bug PRs #1722-#1729 + 9 Cursor PRs #1710-#1721, all trails zero; follow-up #1730; 2 leftover repro repos to delete\n13\t- [PR author not entire app](pr-author-not-entire-app.md) — gh pr create as the user BEFORE entire trail create, else PR author = app/entire bot\n14\t- [git-meta strategic context](git-meta-strategic-context.md) — git-meta.com = James's fast raw K/V-over-git layer; MCP/CLI/web clients on top; brain builds on it; user = first client driver; \"what to store\" is open human design call\n15\t- [Checkpoint-analysis model eval](checkpoint-analysis-model-eval.md) — Fireworks swap for entire-api checkpoint analysis; DeepSeek V4 Flash = fair-eval parity vs Haiku (~7x cheaper); entire-api #333 READY (not merged) + fleet #3312 draft\n16\t- [entire-loop plugin state](entire-loop-plugin-state.md) — self-planning agent-org Entire plugin; full graph-org (edges/converge/router/verifier/clone-isolated mutating build/LLM control plane) built+live-verified+INSTALLED 2026-07-21 (main @7b46264)\n17\t- [Graph SWE-bench verdict](graph-swebench-verdict.md) — MEASURED: graph = token win (−19-23% vs whole-file-naive), NOT accuracy lever (~0, noise); tests-first enrichment backfired + reverted\n18\t- [GraphMark rename+audit state](graphmark-rename-audit-state.md) — entirehq/graphmark PRs #48 (entire-sem→entire-graph rename) + #49 (suite-3 agentic-swebench integrity audit); open, awaiting review, NOT merged\n19\t- [lean-mode measured verdict](lean-mode-measured-verdict.md) — public skill repo suhaanthayyil/lean-mode; MEASURED (120 runs): best −17.3% total/−12.3% cost via TURN reduction; −37% impact/−67% multi-hop but +35% WORSE on named-file; terse-output does NOT cut output; `real` metric is cache-warmth contaminated\n20\t- [Statusline graph badge](statusline-graph-badge.md) — badge \"swaps\" because per-session by default; fixed w/ project scope + committed transcript-digest cache-key fix (eg 6922847); 243K was the caveman token badge, not graph\n21\t- [Token-saver for agents](token-saver-agents.md) — author every subagent/workflow prompt to return caveman-ultra + use RTK; compress style not substance; can't retrofit bundled workflows\n22\t- [Reproduce-proven-results doctrine](reproduce-proven-results-doctrine.md) — standing 2026-07-28: every task = already-achieved work, reproduce it; \"no/impossible\" never a terminal answer, go deeper; always graph+brain+RTK+caveman\n23\t- [Beat-CMM variance verdict](beat-cmm-variance-verdict.md) — eg BEATS cmm per-language on Python (3× −71.4% vs −64.0%, +7.4pt) & C via search-only+sparse-fix (fb7); loses Rust/PHP/Java/Go (type-resolution); cmm wins polyglot aggregate. Single-run signals = ±40-90pt/repo noise, need 3× means\n24\t- [Agentic token saving is the clamp](agentic-token-saving-is-the-clamp.md) — CAUSAL 2026-07-29: eg's SWE-bench token win is the frugality prompt, not the graph; remove clamp → −25.8% becomes −0.9% and eg loses to cmm; eg-only resolve wins = 0\n25\t- [Reclaim disk before heavy runs](reclaim-disk-before-heavy-runs.md) — run reclaim.sh BEFORE grading batches; cmm cache hit 124GB and filled the volume, killing dockerd mid-run (161GB reclaimed)\n26\t- [Graph savings scale with session length](graph-savings-scale-with-session-length.md) — MEASURED: eg saves by deleting locate turns, so ≥35% is unreachable on short-session tiers (haiku −11.6% artifact-free, opus +14.1%); partial-cell and turn-cap bias both inflate the number\n27\t- [CLI turn-start hook latency fix](cli-turnstart-hook-latency-fix.md) — UserPromptSubmit 30s timeouts = per-session flock contention; patched+verified on fix/turnstart-hook-latency, UNMERGED\n28\t- [VERIFY block is the lever](verify-block-is-the-lever.md) — INVERTED: a VERIFY line naming a real test runner COSTS ~11 turns vs no VERIFY line (Sonnet 27.6 vs 16.2 at equal difficulty); shipped EG_VERIFY_MODE=off\n29\t- [eg goal WITHDRAWN](eg-goal-met-verdict.md) — the −35.42% \"tie\" was a tie AT THE FLOOR; on a representative 30 eg LOSES resolves (27→23, 19→15) and per-resolved saving is only −1.2%/−5.3%; removing the prompt asymmetry sends Sonnet to +9.1%\n30\t- [Never stop until goal met](never-stop-until-goal-met.md) — keep running unattended until the goal actually holds; \"no way\" = go one layer deeper (transcripts, harness, graph source), never a terminal answer\n31\t- [Retrieval rank is the lever](retrieval-rank-is-the-lever.md) — eg outcome is a step function of gold-file rank; recall was 70% because EG_TOPK=5 discarded found hits + no file-dedupe/test-drop; fixed config → 93.3%\n32\t- [codeLikeSearchWeight digit bug](codelike-weight-digit-bug.md) — entire-graph scored \"SIM201\" as a 3-letter acronym (1.4), failing the >=2 gate for the exact-code-token bonus; ruff gold went not-found→rank 2; fixed + regression-clean on 30\n33\t- [rep30 single-run noise](rep30-single-run-noise.md) — one 30-instance cell CANNOT resolve config differences: same-instance spread across cells is 45pt median, all Sonnet CIs span zero; trust offline replays, not single-session attributions\n34\t- [Graph savings vs session length](graph-savings-vs-session-length.md) — pooled n=175 corr −0.238 [−0.346,−0.134]: costs money under 12 baseline turns (+11.8%), peaks −30.7% at 20–29, tapers to −21.0% at 50+. NOT monotonic, weak per-cell. Predicts Opus (−0.5pt) + Haiku (+1.9pt) but MISSES SONNET BY +23.9pt — not a complete mechanism. Raising the turn cap does NOT help. Prefetch rejected.\n35\t- [eg cost mechanism](eg-cost-mechanism.md) — \"95% cache_read\" is token COUNT not cost (cache_read is 22–46% of cost; output 25–39%). Tool saves only when it cuts OUTPUT: Haiku all three down (−24.1%), Fable reads −14% but writes +15% → +14.9%. Payload bytes ≈1% of cost, genuinely free.\n\n... [14 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6a80ff87-2ab0-4d0e-9107-24fdc797159b","timestamp":"2026-08-02T13:59:18.658Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"6a80ff87-2ab0-4d0e-9107-24fdc797159b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- graph-bench-forensics: Measure whether a code-intelligence tool (entire-graph, cmm, any retrieval MCP) actually saves an agent tokens, by reading every session transcript and decomposing tool calls into token cost. Use when benchmarking a tool arm against a no-tool baseline, when a token-savings claim needs verifying or reproducing, or when a measured saving disagrees with a previous result.\n- entire-graph:stats: Report how much this repo's coding-agent sessions used the entire-graph code graph versus grep/read exploration, and the estimated tokens that saved. Use when the user asks \"how much did the graph save\", \"token savings\", \"graph usage\", \"am I actually using the graph\", or invokes /entire-graph:stats. Read-only, local, no network.","skillCount":2,"isInitial":false,"names":["graph-bench-forensics","entire-graph:stats"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"196a8717-5c60-45ef-aaff-c833bed6c621","timestamp":"2026-08-02T13:59:18.658Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
