{"parentUuid":"c8ab2791-e506-4900-be29-4fda5dd3fe71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cde4Xw6sxLHb5dwmxjWEA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recon complete. The picture is sharp — and one finding changes the plan:\n\n**#75's branch predates main's whole P1 layer.** It's 84 behind; `internal/{brainwire,factsync,hostedbrain,factmerge}` (merged via #59/#60/#64) don't exist on it. Also **M1.3/M1.4 have no written spec** — one sentence at `brain_wire_contract.md:113` names them; recon derived the implementation-grade rules (no HTML escaping, lexicographic field order, normative `omitempty`, UTC time policy, integer/string canon).\n\nSo \"complete P0+P1 into #75\" = merge main in first (11 conflicts, 9 product), *then* build. Launching both chains:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5061,"cache_read_input_tokens":515538,"output_tokens":9897,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5061},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9897,"cache_read_input_tokens":515538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5061,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cde4XsnwrqaV1me1RqEak","type":"assistant","uuid":"9ac342ed-4753-4789-b2d6-5d3b7a3abf9a","timestamp":"2026-08-02T14:15:23.267Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"9ac342ed-4753-4789-b2d6-5d3b7a3abf9a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cde4Xw6sxLHb5dwmxjWEA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKf4RYMKwyDfkedPXDFBUw","name":"Workflow","input":{"description":"Complete P0+P1 into both PRs","script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'p0-p1-completion',\n  description: 'Land all remaining P0 and P1 work into entire-brain #75 and entire-api #242 worktrees',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Rebase', detail: 'merge main into both PR branches, resolve conflicts' },\n    { title: 'Build', detail: 'implement M1.3, M1.4, transport+CLI, fold #73/#74, api server side' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'build, test, vet, gofmt on both trees' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst BW = '/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-75'\nconst AW = '/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242'\n\nconst RULES = `\nOUTPUT RULES: caveman-terse report — no preamble/filler. State exactly what you changed (file paths + what), what you verified (command + result), and anything you could NOT do. Never claim a build/test passed unless you ran it and saw it pass. If blocked, say so plainly and leave the tree in a compiling state.\nHARD CONSTRAINTS: work ONLY inside the given worktree path. Commit your own work with a clear conventional-commit message. NEVER add AI/Claude/session footers or Co-Authored-By lines to commits. Do NOT push. Do NOT touch any other checkout.`\n\n// ---------- BRAIN CHAIN (sequential, same worktree) ----------\nasync function brainChain() {\n  const r1 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (git worktree of entireio/entire-brain, branch p0p1/brain-75, currently at PR #75 head 923b8a91). It is 84 commits BEHIND entireio/main (afe7d3f2) and 120 ahead.\n\nTASK: merge entireio/main into this branch and resolve every conflict correctly.\n\nRun: cd ${BW} && git merge entireio/main\nExpect 11 content conflicts:\n- PRODUCT code (9): docs/getting-started.md, internal/cli/agent_surface.go, embed_rank.go, embed_rank_test.go, embed_store_test.go, embed_vec_cgo.go, facts_read_cmd.go, mcp.go, retrieve.go\n- BENCHMARK harness (2): benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py (18 hunks), run_test.py\n\nRESOLUTION DOCTRINE — this matters more than speed:\n- Main is authoritative for REFACTORS/MOVES. Main extracted merge logic out of internal/cli into new packages internal/{brainwire,factmerge,factsync,hostedbrain}; the branch still has the pre-extraction copies. Keep main's structure.\n- The branch is authoritative for its NEW FEATURES (brain_brief compact v1/v2/v3, git-intent overlay, action-relevance gate, stale-index bridge, semantic freshness/dedupe, history legacy identity, semantic test suggestions). Preserve them, re-pointed at main's package layout.\n- docs/getting-started.md: main deliberately REDUCED this to a 12-line stub pointing at README.md (content moved into README). Take MAIN's stub; do not resurrect the 650 deleted lines. The branch's only edit there is a 14-line packet_format paragraph — move that content into the correct current home (README.md or docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md), do not re-inflate the stub.\n- For the two python benchmark files: take the union of behavior; when a hunk is a pure conflict of two rewrites, prefer the branch's newer harness logic but keep any main-side fix the branch lacks.\n\nAfter resolving: cd ${BW} && gofmt -l internal/ | head, then go build ./... and go vet ./internal/... — all must be clean. Then commit (conventional message, e.g. \"merge: bring branch up to main (P1 package layout)\"). Report per-file how you resolved each of the 11.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:1-merge-main', phase: 'Rebase', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const r2 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain, now merged up to main). Previous step: ${String(r1).slice(0, 1500)}\n\nTASK: fold in PR #74's local git-meta fact store AND fix its two known CI breaks.\n\n1. Bring in branch entireio/feat/facts-gitmeta-local (17 files, +2668): internal/factgitmeta/** (backend.go, localrepo.go, gitmeta/ vendored engine + tests), internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go, the internal/cli/facts_admin_cmd.go one-liner, and the go.mod/go.sum additions (go-git/v6, go-billy/v6, x/sys bump, termenv promotion).\n   Easiest correct route: cd ${BW} && git cherry-pick 6b2244a9 217d0ad4 bdd7ee33   (resolve any conflicts against the new package layout; internal/factgitmeta implements the internal/factsync Server seam — keep that wiring intact).\n2. FIX CI BREAK 1 — Windows: internal/factgitmeta/localrepo.go uses syscall.Flock/LOCK_EX which is unix-only and breaks build(windows,amd64) + test(windows-latest) + phase1-semantic(windows-latest). Split into lock_unix.go (//go:build !windows) and lock_windows.go (//go:build windows) using LockFileEx/UnlockFileEx from golang.org/x/sys/windows (already an available dep). Same exported behavior on both.\n3. FIX CI BREAK 2 — gofmt: internal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go is unformatted (two one-line goroutine bodies ~line 284). Run gofmt -w on it.\n\nVERIFY: go build ./... ; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... ; go test ./internal/factgitmeta/... -count=1 ; gofmt -l internal/ (must be empty) ; go vet ./internal/... . All must pass — the windows cross-build is the whole point of fix 1. Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:2-fold-pr74', phase: 'Build', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const r3 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain). Prior steps done: merged to main, folded PR #74.\n\nTASK: implement **P1.M1.3 — canonical encoding** for the brain wire artifact, in package internal/brainwire.\n\nThe ONLY existing spec is docs/brain_wire_contract.md:103-114 — read it first. It names 4 hazards that a canonical encoding must close: Go HTML escaping, struct field order, omitempty, RFC3339Nano time. Types to cover (internal/brainwire/contract.go): BrainArtifact, BrainManifest, ContentRef, SnapshotRef, OverlayRef, FactsRef.\n\nImplement internal/brainwire/canonical.go with (at minimum) CanonicalMarshal(a BrainArtifact) ([]byte, error) implementing these rules:\n1. HTML escaping OFF (raw UTF-8; json.Encoder+SetEscapeHTML(false) or hand-emit). Affects repo_key, default_branch, branch, path, media_type, provider.\n2. Object keys ordered LEXICOGRAPHICALLY by JSON tag (RFC 8785 / JCS rule), NOT Go declaration order.\n3. omitempty made normative + exhaustive: per field, define the omitted default (\"\" / 0 / nil / len==0); a producer emitting \"size\":0 or \"tree\":\"\" is non-canonical and MUST be normalized to omission. Empty slice and null both omit.\n4. Time: GeneratedAt → UTC, fixed fractional policy, literal Z suffix (never +00:00). State and enforce the policy (truncate-to-second recommended); document whether sub-second input truncates or errors.\n5. Numbers: decimal integer only — no exponent, no leading zeros, no +, no -0.\n6. Strings: UTF-8, minimal escaping (only \", \\\\, C0 controls; short forms \\\\b \\\\f \\\\n \\\\r \\\\t; remaining C0 as lowercase \\\\u00xx).\nDO NOT change any existing JSON tag — contract.go:14-16 says \"the JSON tags are the contract\"; a tag change would be a major bump.\n\nAlso add CanonicalUnmarshal or a Canonicalize(raw []byte) ([]byte,error) that normalizes foreign (non-Go-produced) bytes into canonical form, since the point is cross-implementation.\n\nTESTS (internal/brainwire/canonical_test.go) proving each rule: idempotence (Canonical(Canonical(x))==Canonical(x)); order-independence (two field orders → identical bytes); explicit \"size\":0 / \"tree\":\"\" normalized away; HTML chars unescaped; time with and without sub-second → identical bytes; a golden byte-fixture. Table-driven, in the style of the existing tests.\n\nVERIFY: go test ./internal/brainwire/... -count=1 -race ; go build ./... ; gofmt -l internal/ empty ; go vet ./internal/brainwire/... . Update docs/brain_wire_contract.md to replace the \"M1.3/M1.4 define...\" forward-reference with the now-defined rules. Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:3-m1.3-canonical', phase: 'Build', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const r4 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain). M1.3 canonical encoding now exists in internal/brainwire (see: ${String(r3).slice(0, 1200)}).\n\nTASK: implement **P1.M1.4 — cross-implementation manifest signing**, building ON TOP of the M1.3 canonical encoding.\n\nRead docs/brain_wire_contract.md (esp. the integrity section) first. Design constraints from it: blobs are ALREADY content-addressed by sha256: digest, so signing covers the MANIFEST, not blob bytes; signatures must be verifiable by a non-Go implementation, which is exactly why canonical encoding (M1.3) is the substrate.\n\nImplement in internal/brainwire (e.g. signing.go):\n- Sign(manifest, signer) producing a detached signature over the CANONICAL bytes of the manifest (ed25519; state the algorithm identifier in the signature envelope so it can rotate).\n- Verify(manifest, signature, pubkey) with clear error types for: bad signature, unknown algorithm, key mismatch, non-canonical input.\n- A signature envelope struct with explicit fields (alg, key id, sig, and the canonical-encoding version it was produced under) so a future encoding change cannot silently validate.\n- Key handling: load from file/env, never log key material, and make the API take an interface (crypto.Signer) rather than raw bytes where practical.\n- The manifest signature MUST commit to every blob digest it references (so swapping a blob invalidates the signature) — verify that property explicitly.\n\nTESTS: sign→verify round trip; tampered manifest fails; tampered/added/removed blob digest fails; wrong key fails; unknown alg fails; signature stable across two independent canonical marshals; golden fixture.\n\nVERIFY: go test ./internal/brainwire/... -count=1 -race ; go build ./... ; gofmt -l internal/ empty ; go vet ./internal/brainwire/... . Document the scheme in docs/brain_wire_contract.md. Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:4-m1.4-signing', phase: 'Build', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const r5 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain). TASK: close the two explicit PR #64 deferrals.\n\nRead first: internal/factsync/{sync.go,httpserver.go,review.go,egress.go}, internal/factmerge/admin.go (ApplyProposal/RejectProposal/Promote), internal/hostedbrain/*.\n\n**(A) Open-proposal-set HTTP transport.** Today internal/factsync/httpserver.go implements only GET /api/v1/repos/{repoID}/brain/facts?branch=… and POST …/brain/facts/advance (200 / 412 PreconditionFailed / 409 Conflict). The proposal MODEL and Resolve are implemented and proven (TestCrossMemberConflictRoutedThenResolvedConverges) but the proposal set has NO transport. Add it, symmetric with the existing style:\n - list open proposals for a repo/branch\n - fetch one proposal\n - apply / reject a proposal (mapping to factmerge.ApplyProposal / RejectProposal)\n - correct status codes incl. 412/409 semantics already used, and egress redaction applied consistently with internal/factsync/egress.go\n - client side in internal/hostedbrain so a hosted brain can drive it\n Keep the Server interface seam (internal/factsync/sync.go:45) intact — internal/factgitmeta implements it.\n\n**(B) Wire hostedbrain/factsync into user-facing CLI verbs.** They are currently reachable only programmatically. Add the CLI surface under internal/cli consistent with existing command style and registration (see internal/cli/root.go and facts_sync_cmd.go): list/show/apply/reject open proposals, and make the hosted path opt-in exactly like publish.go does (two-gate, ADR-P1-A; hosted disabled unless explicitly enabled — do NOT change default behavior or enable egress by default).\n\nTESTS: handler tests for every new endpoint incl. error/status paths; client tests; CLI command tests following the existing table-driven style; a round-trip test proving propose→list→apply converges.\n\nVERIFY: go test ./internal/factsync/... ./internal/hostedbrain/... ./internal/factmerge/... ./internal/cli/... -count=1 ; go build ./... ; gofmt -l internal/ empty ; go vet ./internal/... . Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:5-transport-cli', phase: 'Build', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const r6 = await agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain). TASK: finish **P0**.\n\n1. **Fold in PR #73's docs content** (branch entireio/docs/p0m5-install-docs, 2 files +372/-104): docs/release_press_release.md takes PR #73's version wholesale (accuracy pass vs shipped v0.1.0). For docs/getting-started.md, note main has deliberately stubbed it to point at README.md — so put PR #73's cold-start install + first-run content in the place main's layout expects (README.md), NOT by re-inflating the stub. Preserve all of #73's substance: requirements, install (go install: provider entire-graph then brain; from source; release archive), verify, first run/build+query a brain, missing-provider path, query, optional distill facts, use from an agent, what you get, further reading. Keep post-rename naming (entire graph, never entire sem).\n2. **Reconcile docs/ga-readiness.md gates 9 and 10.** The table marks them ⏳ but the resolved section marks them ✅ (gate 9: 0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 provenance on the RC SHA; gate 10: both repos tagged v0.1.0 on the aligned GA SHA). Read both regions, make the doc self-consistent based on the evidence it itself cites, and note the P0.M5 line is now satisfied by the docs landing in this PR.\n3. If the doc claims a release/install command that cannot work (module path on main is github.com/ashtom/entire-brain, so go install github.com/entireio/... will not resolve), keep the accurate fallback wording — do NOT print a command that fails.\n\nVERIFY: no broken relative links in touched docs (grep the link targets exist); go build ./... still clean. Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'brain:6-p0-docs', phase: 'Build', effort: 'medium' })\n\n  return { r1, r2, r3, r4, r5, r6 }\n}\n\n// ---------- API CHAIN (sequential, same worktree) ----------\nasync function apiChain() {\n  const a1 = await agent(`Worktree ${AW} (git worktree of entirehq/entire-api, branch p0p1/api-242, at PR #242 head df65014a \"docs(adr): 0005 EntireDB storage push-down (P1.M7 RFD)\"). PR #242 is CONFLICTING/DIRTY vs origin/main (+8891/-2, 61 files).\n\nTASK: merge origin/main into this branch and resolve all conflicts.\n\nRun: cd ${AW} && git fetch origin --quiet && git merge origin/main\nResolve every conflict. Doctrine: main is authoritative for anything it refactored/moved; this branch is authoritative for its new P1 server surface — internal/brainbuild/** (fact_sync, fact_advance_log, fact_ref_index, overlay_branch_index, coordinate_lock, policy, worker, store_seams), internal/brainquery/**, internal/brainstore/**, docs/adr/0004-brain-tenancy-is-repo-tenancy.md, docs/adr/0005-entiredb-storage-push-down.md, .env.example. Preserve both sides' intent; never delete a main-side fix.\n\nVERIFY: cd ${AW} && go build ./... && go vet ./internal/... && gofmt -l internal/ | head (must be empty). If the repo has a mise task for lint/test, note it but do NOT run Docker-dependent integration tests. Commit. Report each conflict and how you resolved it.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'api:1-merge-main', phase: 'Rebase', effort: 'high' })\n\n  const a2 = await agent(`Worktree ${AW} (entire-api, merged up to main). Prior: ${String(a1).slice(0, 1200)}\n\nTASK: add the SERVER-side counterparts that complete P1, mirroring what the brain client now expects.\n\nRead first: internal/brainbuild/fact_sync.go, internal/brainstore/**, internal/brainquery/**, httpapi/ (find the brain routes: grep -rn \"brain\" httpapi/ internal/httpapi 2>/dev/null | head -30), docs/adr/0004 and 0005.\n\nAdd, consistent with this repo's existing Huma/chi handler + store patterns:\n1. **Open-proposal-set endpoints** — the server half of the brain-side transport: list open proposals, get one, apply, reject; scoped by repo (and branch where the model is branch-scoped). Reuse the existing tenancy/authz middleware — brain tenancy IS repo tenancy per ADR-0004; do not invent a new scope. Status codes must match the existing fact-sync contract (200 / 409 conflict / 412 precondition-failed).\n2. **Manifest integrity on ingest** — where the server accepts a brain artifact/fact-set, verify the content-addressed blob digests it references, and reject a payload whose manifest does not match its referenced digests. (The brain side now signs the manifest over a canonical encoding; the server must at minimum enforce digest consistency and MUST NOT silently accept a mismatch.)\n3. Migrations if new tables/columns are required — use the repo's migration convention exactly (goose, embedded, UTC-timestamp filenames via scripts/new-migration.sh; NEVER hand-pick integers, never edit a merged migration).\n\nTESTS: handler tests for every endpoint incl. authz-denied and error paths, following existing test style. Skip anything requiring a live Postgres if the harness needs Docker — write the test so it skips cleanly without a DB (match how existing *_pg_test.go files gate themselves).\n\nVERIFY: go build ./... ; go vet ./internal/... ; gofmt -l internal/ empty ; go test ./internal/brainbuild/... ./internal/brainstore/... ./internal/brainquery/... -count=1 (non-Docker only). Commit.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'api:2-server-p1', phase: 'Build', effort: 'high' })\n\n  return { a1, a2 }\n}\n\nphase('Rebase')\nconst [brain, api] = await parallel([brainChain, apiChain])\n\nphase('Verify')\nconst checks = await parallel([\n  () => agent(`Worktree ${BW} (entire-brain) — FINAL VERIFICATION. Do not add features; verify and fix only what is broken.\nRun and report exact output tails: (1) go build ./... (2) GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... (3) go vet ./internal/... (4) gofmt -l internal/ cmd/ (5) go test ./internal/... -count=1 (report pass/fail counts; list any FAILING package + the first failure message).\nIf anything fails, FIX it minimally and re-run until green, then commit the fix. If a failure is pre-existing on entireio/main (check by testing the same package at main), say so and leave it.\nFinally: git log --oneline entireio/codex/benchmark-repair-integration..HEAD and git diff --stat entireio/codex/benchmark-repair-integration..HEAD | tail -3 — report what this work added on top of the PR head.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'verify:brain', phase: 'Verify', effort: 'high' }),\n  () => agent(`Worktree ${AW} (entire-api) — FINAL VERIFICATION. Do not add features; verify and fix only what is broken.\nRun and report exact output tails: (1) go build ./... (2) go vet ./internal/... (3) gofmt -l internal/ (4) go test ./internal/... -count=1 -short (report pass/fail; list failing packages; note which need Docker/Postgres and are skipped).\nIf anything fails, FIX minimally and re-run until green, then commit. If a failure is pre-existing on origin/main, verify that and say so.\nFinally: git log --oneline origin/m4-brain-auth..HEAD and git diff --stat origin/m4-brain-auth..HEAD | tail -3.${RULES}`,\n    { label: 'verify:api', phase: 'Verify', effort: 'high' }),\n])\n\nreturn { brain, api, checks }\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5061,"cache_read_input_tokens":515538,"output_tokens":9897,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5061},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9897,"cache_read_input_tokens":515538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5061,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cde4XsnwrqaV1me1RqEak","type":"assistant","uuid":"fb99d5d8-955f-4f33-bd36-15b6bbf50601","timestamp":"2026-08-02T14:17:00.018Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","s