{"parentUuid":"3568d0c4-6921-4ad2-991a-d3e9cf277127","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdeB2Cxbc9yZr1FN8dDVa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# P0 + P1 complete — built, green, not pushed\n\n## The finding that shaped it\n**#75's branch was 84 behind main and missing main's entire P1 layer** — `internal/{brainwire,factsync,hostedbrain,factmerge}` (from merged #59/#60/#64) simply weren't on it. M1.3/M1.4 extend those packages, so nothing could be built until main was merged in first. Also: **M1.3/M1.4 had no spec** — one sentence at `brain_wire_contract.md:113`. I derived the rules from the 4 hazards it names.\n\n## #75 / entire-brain — 6 commits (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-75`)\n| commit | what |\n|---|---|\n| `723eec23` | merge main — **11 conflicts resolved**, 9 product + 2 benchmark-python |\n| `666c…`→`3bd2…` | folded PR #74's `internal/factgitmeta` (cherry-picked clean) |\n| `47bd6932` | **fixed #74's 2 CI breaks** — flock split to `lock_unix.go`/`lock_windows.go` (`windows.LockFileEx`), gofmt |\n| `6418f74f` | **M1.3 canonical encoding** — `CanonicalMarshal` / `Canonicalize` / `CanonicalUnmarshal`; HTML-escaping off, lexicographic keys, normative `omitempty`, UTC-Z time, integer/minimal-escape rules, zero JSON-tag changes |\n| `a3bfc2ea` | **M1.4 manifest signing** — ed25519, versioned `Signature` envelope (alg + key id + encoding version), `ReferencedDigests` so the sig commits to every blob digest |\n| `ac96f01e` | **#64's deferrals** — `factsync/httpproposals.go` (list/get/apply/resolve), `hostedbrain` client, CLI `facts proposals {list,show,apply,reject}` |\n| `5ce71176` | **P0** — #73's docs folded into main's README layout (not re-inflating the stub main deliberately shrank), `ga-readiness.md` gates 9+10 ⏳→✅ |\n\n## #242 / entire-api — 2 commits (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242`)\n`ce0fc79c` merge origin/main · `eb522950` server side: `brainbuild/proposals.go` + `proposal_index{,_pg}.go`, `httpapi/brain_proposals.go`, `brainstore/validate.go` (manifest/blob-digest integrity on ingest), migration `20260802142559_brain_fact_proposals.sql` via the goose UTC convention.\n\n## Gates — I ran these myself, not taking the agents' word\n**brain:** `go build` ✓ · **`GOOS=windows` cross-build ✓** · `go vet ./...` ✓ · `gofmt -l` empty · `go test ./...` **all 9 packages ok** · brainwire `-race` ok\n**api:** build ✓ · vet ✓ · brainbuild + brainstore + brainquery + httpapi tests ok · the 5 `gofmt` offenders are **pre-existing on main**, none ours\n\n## Two things needing your eyes (not mechanical)\n1. **`run.py` adherence semantics** — main *excludes* adherence-invalid runs from arm means, the branch *retained* them. I took main's (it has the asserting test; the branch has none). That's a methodology call on your benchmark.\n2. **`facts_default_retrieval_test.go` goldens moved** — main's `semanticResultMask` genuinely tightens reachability on the branch's corpus. Verified it's main's mask, not my fusion-depth cap.\n\n## Not done — your call\n**Nothing is pushed.** #242 is yours; **#75 is ashtom's branch**, and this adds ~23.7K lines across 163 files to a draft that was already 552 files. My honest recommendation stands: land the P0/P1 work as **its own PR off main** (it's clean and self-contained now) and let #75 stay the brief-retrieval PR. Say the word and I'll push either way — same commits, different target."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":548826,"output_tokens":1420,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":538},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1420,"cache_read_input_tokens":548826,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_t