{"parentUuid":"20664497-e0bf-4254-87eb-c60e63d4e10e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5PqrxuFntSiMy6WWAnw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495016,"cache_read_input_tokens":22119,"output_tokens":3631,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1642},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495016,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3631,"cache_read_input_tokens":22119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495016},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011Ce5PqpxrFkSKxG5otFhPo","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba61dc94-d3d2-452d-a616-2b9636bd1335","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:23:26.559Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ba61dc94-d3d2-452d-a616-2b9636bd1335","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5PqrxuFntSiMy6WWAnw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the whole picture, and the ordered list to finish P0 then P1.\n\n## Where things actually stand\n\nAll the remaining code is **written, verified, and green** — but it lives in two local worktrees, unpushed. Nothing is merged. So the todo list below is mostly *landing* work, not *building* work.\n\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-75` — 6 commits (P0 docs + M1.3 + M1.4 + #64 deferrals + PR #74 folded and CI-fixed)\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242` — 2 commits (merge + server-side proposals/integrity/migration)\n\n---\n\n# P0 — finish (local brain GA)\n\nGates 1–11 are satisfied except the documentation item. Three things left.\n\n**P0-1. Decide where the docs land** ← *your call, blocks everything else*\nPR #73 raises `docs/getting-started.md` to 250 lines. But main deliberately **stubbed that file to 12 lines** and moved the content into README. So #73 is semantically stale even though git says mergeable. My commit `5ce71176` already resolves this the right way: same content, folded into README where main's layout expects it.\n- Option A: push my version, close #73 as superseded\n- Option B: merge #73 as-is, then fix the layout afterward\nI recommend A.\n\n**P0-2. Reconcile `ga-readiness.md` gates 9 and 10** ✅ *already done in `5ce71176`*\nTable said ⏳, resolved section said ✅. Now both say ✅ with the evidence cited (0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 provenance; both repos tagged v0.1.0 on the aligned SHA).\n\n**P0-3. Close the three install-truth blockers** ← *real GA blockers, not cosmetic*\n1. **Module path is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`**, so the documented `go install github.com/entireio/entire-brain/...@v0.1.0` cannot resolve. Either rename the module path or keep the source-install fallback. A rename is a breaking change and needs your decision.\n2. `entire plugin install` doesn't resolve the `requires: sem` provider dependency, so provider install stays manual.\n3. Confirm the v0.1.0 release archive actually ships a provider that answers `entire graph`.\n\n**P0 is done when:** docs land, gates read consistently, and the install path in the docs is one a new user can actually run.\n\n---\n\n# P1 — finish (shared/hosted brain)\n\n**Already merged on main:** M1.1 wire contract (#59), M1.5 publish client (#60), M2.2 merge engine, M2.3 fact-sync runner, M2.4 conflict routing, M3.3 remote MCP client (all #64).\n\n**P1-1. Land the brain half** — built, green, unpushed\n- M1.3 canonical encoding (`internal/brainwire/canonical.go`)\n- M1.4 manifest signing (`signing.go`, ed25519, signature commits to every blob digest)\n- #64's deferred open-proposal HTTP transport + `facts proposals {list,show,apply,reject}` CLI\n- PR #74's `internal/factgitmeta` folded in, with its two CI breaks fixed (Windows flock split, gofmt)\n\n**P1-2. Land the api half** — built, green, unpushed\nPR #242 plus my commit: proposal endpoints under existing repo tenancy, manifest/blob-digest integrity on ingest, migration `20260802142559_brain_fact_proposals.sql`.\n\n**P1-3. Land git-meta-service PR #1**\nThat's the engine brain currently vendors verbatim. Once it lands, brain can de-vendor `internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/` instead of carrying a copy.\n\n**P1-4. Live cross-repo round-trip** ← *the one thing never actually executed*\n#64 explicitly deferred it: brain client against a running entire-api, end to end. Everything is proven in isolation with fakes; the real wire has never been exercised. This is the highest-value remaining verification.\n\n**P1-5. Unblock shared publication** ← *external, not ours*\nBlocked in entiredb: `refs/meta/*` pushes are denylisted in `server/githttp/receive_pack.go`, and the read-only `git-meta` service identity isn't registered. Until that lands, the fact store is local-only by design.\n\n**P1-6. Deploy runbook**\nStaging: run migrations, flip `ENTIRE_BRAIN_HOSTED_ENABLED`, smoke, then prod.\n\n**Not started, and arguably out of scope:** M1.2's server store is what #242 *is*. There are no M4–M7 milestones defined anywhere in the repo despite the naming — only the P1.M7 RFD doc (ADR-0005) exists.\n\n---\n\n## Two things worth flagging before any of this merges\n\n1. **`run.py` adherence semantics** — I took main's \"exclude adherence-invalid runs from arm means\" over the branch's \"retain\". Main has the asserting test, the branch has none. That's a benchmark methodology call, yours to confirm.\n2. **`facts_default_retrieval_test.go` goldens moved** — main's `semanticResultMask` genuinely tightens reachability on that corpus. Verified it's main's change, not mine.\n\n---\n\n## What I can do without asking vs what needs you\n\n**I can do now:** push the api-242 work to your own `m4-brain-auth` branch; de-vendor git-meta once #1 lands; write the round-trip test harness.\n\n**Needs your decision:** P0-1 (where docs land), P0-3.1 (module rename), pushing to **#75** (ashtom's branch — and my recommendation remains a fresh PR off main instead, since the work is clean and self-contained while #75 is a 552-file conflicted draft).\n\nWhich do you want first: push api-242, or open the clean brain PR off main?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495016,"cache_read_input_tokens":22119,"output_tokens":3631,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1642},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495016,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3631,"cache_read_input_tokens":22119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495016},"type":"message"}],"spe