{"parentUuid":"f143b5bb-84da-417b-8b38-4ae992ff9db6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5PyauUbYJ4VFaamsngy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FQgzDF7BfnbpdZJQ2VTdjd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"=== entire-graph PR #104 ===\"\ngh pr view 104 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json number,title,state,isDraft,mergeable,mergedAt,additions,deletions,changedFiles,headRefName,baseRefName,body --jq '\"#\\(.number) [\\(.state)] draft=\\(.isDraft) \\(.title)\\nbranch=\\(.headRefName)->\\(.baseRefName) +\\(.additions)/-\\(.deletions) files=\\(.changedFiles) merged=\\(.mergedAt//\"-\")\\n---BODY---\\n\\(.body[0:2500])\"' 2>&1 | head -60","description":"Read entire-graph PR 104"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3782,"cache_read_input_tokens":517135,"output_tokens":2909,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2580},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3782,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2909,"cache_read_input_tokens":517135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3782},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5PyYMSGg9N7WYf8vyz4","type":"assistant","uuid":"db2a5e10-5340-4d3a-a891-5854701751f7","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:25:18.078Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"db2a5e10-5340-4d3a-a891-5854701751f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"97dfe4e4-11a4-4e75-b97a-5c9aecc36707","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FQgzDF7BfnbpdZJQ2VTdjd","type":"tool_result","content":"=== entire-graph PR #104 ===\n#104 [OPEN] draft=false feat(search): prose retrieval by section, with the benchmark kit that measures it\nbranch=feat/prose-retrieval-and-benchmarks->main +5172/-33 files=28 merged=-\n---BODY---\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/55\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nTwo retrieval fixes for prose, plus the benchmark kit that measures them. Supersedes #100, #103\nand #101, which are closed in favour of this.\n\nCode is `internal/sem` only (438 insertions); everything else is `bench/memory/` — docs, adapters\nand patch files. No Go outside the prose path is touched.\n\n---\n\n## The defect\n\n`selectSearchCandidates` admits **one candidate per file**. For code that is right — a file is\nthe thing you open. For prose it is wrong: a markdown document's heading regions already exist in\nthe graph as `section` entities (`parser.go` `markdownEntities`), are already scored, and are then\ncollapsed to one per file.\n\nMeasured on a real prose corpus at `--top-k 200`, the shipped build returned **19 results across\n19 files while carrying 195 passages holding 42 KB of evidence** that no `results[]` consumer\ncould reach. Ranks 6–19 got a one-line snippet.\n\n**Commit 1 — multi-resolution prose retrieval.** When fewer distinct files match than `--top-k`\nasked for, spend the spare slots promoting those regions to results of their own. Strictly\nadditive: runs after selection, only fills slots the distinct-file ranking left empty, never\nbreaches `--max-context-bytes`. `--single-resolution` restores the old output.\n\nThat alone was not enough, because promoted regions are **satellites**: `Score: parent.Score`\nverbatim, ordered by a round-robin over *parent index*, appended after every parent. Result:\n\n```\n200 results  ->  19 distinct scores\n```\n\n181 of 200 are score-duplicates of one of 19 parents. A consumer sorting by score with a stable\nsort therefore gets 19 blocks — one document's parent followed by its regions, then the next.\nTruncate to the top 50/20/10 and you see only the first one or two documents. Evidence that must\nbe stitched across documents structurally cannot surface.\n\n**Commit 2 — rank prose sections as independent candidates.** The retrieval unit becomes the\nsection (`proseParentKey`, keyed by the heading's SymbolID, falling back to file path where a\ndocument has no section structure). A section competes on its own score, as an independent file\nwould. Breadth is preserved: **no document gets a second region until every document that fits\nhas one**, binding every selection pass. `--document-resolution` restores the previous behaviour.\n\nBoth changes are query-blind. The unit comes from the parser's section entities and th","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"53d3ee71-1bc4-4399-8990-b3563a0028c2","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:25:20.020Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== entire-graph PR #104 ===\n#104 [OPEN] draft=false feat(search): prose retrieval by section, with the benchmark kit that measures it\nbranch=feat/prose-retrieval-and-benchmarks->main +5172/-33 files=28 merged=-\n---BODY---\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/55\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nTwo retrieval fixes for prose, plus the benchmark kit that measures them. Supersedes #100, #103\nand #101, which are closed in favour of this.\n\nCode is `internal/sem` only (438 insertions); everything else is `bench/memory/` — docs, adapters\nand patch files. No Go outside the prose path is touched.\n\n---\n\n## The defect\n\n`selectSearchCandidates` admits **one candidate per file**. For code that is right — a file is\nthe thing you open. For prose it is wrong: a markdown document's heading regions already exist in\nthe graph as `section` entities (`parser.go` `markdownEntities`), are already scored, and are then\ncollapsed to one per file.\n\nMeasured on a real prose corpus at `--top-k 200`, the shipped build returned **19 results across\n19 files while carrying 195 passages holding 42 KB of evidence** that no `results[]` consumer\ncould reach. Ranks 6–19 got a one-line snippet.\n\n**Commit 1 — multi-resolution prose retrieval.** When fewer distinct files match than `--top-k`\nasked for, spend the spare slots promoting those regions to results of their own. Strictly\nadditive: runs after selection, only fills slots the distinct-file ranking left empty, never\nbreaches `--max-context-bytes`. `--single-resolution` restores the old output.\n\nThat alone was not enough, because promoted regions are **satellites**: `Score: parent.Score`\nverbatim, ordered by a round-robin over *parent index*, appended after every parent. Result:\n\n```\n200 results  ->  19 distinct scores\n```\n\n181 of 200 are score-duplicates of one of 19 parents. A consumer sorting by score with a stable\nsort therefore gets 19 blocks — one document's parent followed by its regions, then the next.\nTruncate to the top 50/20/10 and you see only the first one or two documents. Evidence that must\nbe stitched across documents structurally cannot surface.\n\n**Commit 2 — rank prose sections as independent candidates.** The retrieval unit becomes the\nsection (`proseParentKey`, keyed by the heading's SymbolID, falling back to file path where a\ndocument has no section structure). A section competes on its own score, as an independent file\nwould. Breadth is preserved: **no document gets a second region until every document that fits\nhas one**, binding every selection pass. `--document-resolution` restores the previous behaviour.\n\nBoth changes are query-blind. The unit comes from the parser's section entities and th","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db2a5e10-5340-4d3a-a891-5854701751f7","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
