{"parentUuid":"eb44c660-6b05-4336-9edc-10e730f9492e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5Q2kUnCESkApumfj1Q5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #104 = prose retrieval by section (multi-resolution). Changes what `search` returns. Checking whether brain's consumption assumes one-result-per-file:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3907,"cache_read_input_tokens":520917,"output_tokens":483,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":233},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3907,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":520917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3907},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5Q2hYAnS367g441R9XL","type":"assistant","uuid":"b79dc0e8-741e-4c0a-919c-1b279fde0bf9","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:25:34.379Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"b79dc0e8-741e-4c0a-919c-1b279fde0bf9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5Q2kUnCESkApumfj1Q5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XfC2T6Kj8abUGbvF3A1Emo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr view 104 --repo entireio/entire-graph --json body --jq .body 2>/dev/null | sed -n '55,120p'\necho \"=== files changed in #104 (code only) ===\"\ngh pr diff 104 --repo entireio/entire-graph --name-only 2>/dev/null | grep -v '^bench/' | head -20","description":"Rest of PR 104 body + code files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3907,"cache_read_input_tokens":520917,"output_tokens":483,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":233},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3907,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":520917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3907},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5Q2hYAnS367g441R9XL","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e1b37dc-6181-4f6a-8c1a-9fc5f060314b","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:25:35.475Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"4e1b37dc-6181-4f6a-8c1a-9fc5f060314b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"97dfe4e4-11a4-4e75-b97a-5c9aecc36707","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XfC2T6Kj8abUGbvF3A1Emo","type":"tool_result","content":"| **after** | **196.0** | **295.3** | **84.9** | **18.9** | **53,929** |\n| off switch | 195.0 | 243.0 | 17.1 | 18.9 | 60,854 |\n\nScore diversity 17.1 → 84.9, document coverage unchanged, and **11.4% fewer bytes** — the old\nbuild computed regions and discarded them unread. The off switch is byte-identical to the\nprevious behaviour on every metric.\n\n## Code search is unaffected\n\n**30 of 30 full-JSON payloads identical** — 15 real locate queries against this repo at\n`--top-k 10` *and* `--top-k 50`, comparing entire payloads (results element by element plus\n`stats`, `commit`, `tree`, `completeness`, `diagnostics`), latency telemetry excluded.\n\nThe prose branch sits behind `proseParentCorpus`, requiring ≥4 units and ≥80% doc-extension\npaths — a source repo cannot reach it. Verified rather than asserted: three deliberately\ndocumentation-flavoured queries against this Go repo returned **zero** results carrying\n`retrieval_mode=prose-parent` in either build.\n\n## Benchmark result\n\nLoCoMo, all 1540 questions, answerer **and** judge both `gpt-5.6-sol`, `top_k=200`, against a\nmem0 OSS control **running concurrently in the same window**. No harness flag, no ingest change —\nthe shipped corpus shape.\n\n| | overall | single-hop | multi-hop | temporal | open-domain |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **entire-graph** | **94.74** | **96.67** | **93.97** | **95.33** | 78.12 |\n| mem0 OSS | 93.83 | 95.12 | 93.62 | 94.70 | **80.21** |\n\n**+0.91pp overall, discordant 43–29, McNemar p = 0.125 — statistically tied, point estimate\nfavours entire-graph.** That wording follows a decision rule registered before the run finished.\n**single-hop +1.55pp, p = 0.035** is the one cell significant on its own.\n\nMulti-hop moved from **−1.44 against mem0 to +0.35** — the deficit this change targets, and the\ncategory the 19-distinct-scores collapse was starving.\n\nThe isolated effect of commit 1, measured paired on the same corpus with the binary as the only\nvariable: **91.56 → 93.83, +2.27pp, discordant 46–11, p = 3.3e-06, n = 1540.**\n\n### Stated plainly\n\n- Run-to-run noise on this harness is **0.65pp** — two identical mem0 runs scored 93.83 and 93.57.\n- entire-graph delivers ~30% more context per question, and **mem0 is more context-efficient\n  below ~25k chars** (43.2 accuracy points per 1k chars at top-10 against our 5.7). `top_k`\n  equalises item count, not context volume.\n- Prose search is **2.1× slower per query** (0.300s → 0.628s); passages are planned for ~196\n  units instead of 19. Code-search latency is unchanged.\n- Open-domain is our one losing category.\n\n## The benchmark kit\n\n`bench/memory/` makes every number above reproducible: the entire-graph adapter, the competitor\nports we wrote, the fairness spec, a run index, and apply-checked patches for the four upstream\nfiles we modified. Upstream is pinned by **md5-verified fork point**, not a guessed SHA, and the\njudge/answerer prompts are byte-identical to upstream — we did not tune the grading.\n\n**Three competitor defects were found and fixed in the competitors' favour**: mem0 **+6.04**\n(a `limit` kwarg silently capping search at 20 memories instead of 200), cognee **+13.77**\n(state on disk with an in-memory retrieval buffer, so resumed runs searched nothing), and cmm\nfrom **structurally zero** (its shipped BM25 excludes `Section` nodes, so prose returns no\nresults). A fourth, against mem0, is disclosed rather than fixed — it is measured at 0.13pp.\n\n## Tests\n\n`mise run check` green. Three regressions were found and fixed during development, each pinned by\na test: whole-document exclusion at small top-k, loss of same-document passages at tight top-k,\n=== files changed in #104 (code only) ===\ninternal/cli/help.go\ninternal/cli/search.go\ninternal/sem/search.go\ninternal/sem/search_multi_resolution.go\ninternal/sem/search_multi_resolution_test.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_parent.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_section_test.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_session_test.go","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4efcf624-693a-4aea-b589-c0a310eefdc5","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:25:37.151Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"| **after** | **196.0** | **295.3** | **84.9** | **18.9** | **53,929** |\n| off switch | 195.0 | 243.0 | 17.1 | 18.9 | 60,854 |\n\nScore diversity 17.1 → 84.9, document coverage unchanged, and **11.4% fewer bytes** — the old\nbuild computed regions and discarded them unread. The off switch is byte-identical to the\nprevious behaviour on every metric.\n\n## Code search is unaffected\n\n**30 of 30 full-JSON payloads identical** — 15 real locate queries against this repo at\n`--top-k 10` *and* `--top-k 50`, comparing entire payloads (results element by element plus\n`stats`, `commit`, `tree`, `completeness`, `diagnostics`), latency telemetry excluded.\n\nThe prose branch sits behind `proseParentCorpus`, requiring ≥4 units and ≥80% doc-extension\npaths — a source repo cannot reach it. Verified rather than asserted: three deliberately\ndocumentation-flavoured queries against this Go repo returned **zero** results carrying\n`retrieval_mode=prose-parent` in either build.\n\n## Benchmark result\n\nLoCoMo, all 1540 questions, answerer **and** judge both `gpt-5.6-sol`, `top_k=200`, against a\nmem0 OSS control **running concurrently in the same window**. No harness flag, no ingest change —\nthe shipped corpus shape.\n\n| | overall | single-hop | multi-hop | temporal | open-domain |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **entire-graph** | **94.74** | **96.67** | **93.97** | **95.33** | 78.12 |\n| mem0 OSS | 93.83 | 95.12 | 93.62 | 94.70 | **80.21** |\n\n**+0.91pp overall, discordant 43–29, McNemar p = 0.125 — statistically tied, point estimate\nfavours entire-graph.** That wording follows a decision rule registered before the run finished.\n**single-hop +1.55pp, p = 0.035** is the one cell significant on its own.\n\nMulti-hop moved from **−1.44 against mem0 to +0.35** — the deficit this change targets, and the\ncategory the 19-distinct-scores collapse was starving.\n\nThe isolated effect of commit 1, measured paired on the same corpus with the binary as the only\nvariable: **91.56 → 93.83, +2.27pp, discordant 46–11, p = 3.3e-06, n = 1540.**\n\n### Stated plainly\n\n- Run-to-run noise on this harness is **0.65pp** — two identical mem0 runs scored 93.83 and 93.57.\n- entire-graph delivers ~30% more context per question, and **mem0 is more context-efficient\n  below ~25k chars** (43.2 accuracy points per 1k chars at top-10 against our 5.7). `top_k`\n  equalises item count, not context volume.\n- Prose search is **2.1× slower per query** (0.300s → 0.628s); passages are planned for ~196\n  units instead of 19. Code-search latency is unchanged.\n- Open-domain is our one losing category.\n\n## The benchmark kit\n\n`bench/memory/` makes every number above reproducible: the entire-graph adapter, the competitor\nports we wrote, the fairness spec, a run index, and apply-checked patches for the four upstream\nfiles we modified. Upstream is pinned by **md5-verified fork point**, not a guessed SHA, and the\njudge/answerer prompts are byte-identical to upstream — we did not tune the grading.\n\n**Three competitor defects were found and fixed in the competitors' favour**: mem0 **+6.04**\n(a `limit` kwarg silently capping search at 20 memories instead of 200), cognee **+13.77**\n(state on disk with an in-memory retrieval buffer, so resumed runs searched nothing), and cmm\nfrom **structurally zero** (its shipped BM25 excludes `Section` nodes, so prose returns no\nresults). A fourth, against mem0, is disclosed rather than fixed — it is measured at 0.13pp.\n\n## Tests\n\n`mise run check` green. Three regressions were found and fixed during development, each pinned by\na test: whole-document exclusion at small top-k, loss of same-document passages at tight top-k,\n=== files changed in #104 (code only) ===\ninternal/cli/help.go\ninternal/cli/search.go\ninternal/sem/search.go\ninternal/sem/search_multi_resolution.go\ninternal/sem/search_multi_resolution_test.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_parent.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_section_test.go\ninternal/sem/search_prose_session_test.go","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e1b37dc-6181-4f6a-8c1a-9fc5f060314b","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
