{"parentUuid":"c707c72c-e36b-4ac7-b242-98ad51f796ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8V4eLqN8o4hX9WLkFiK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U9yNg3iCiFeEKMyoYdA8cP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(facts): make hosted settlements stick and interlock local review\n\nCloses the two review findings that reshaped the model rather than repairing it.\n\nAccepted settlements did not stick. A teammate resolving a conflict on the hosted\nqueue advanced the shared head, but the losing member's local facts were never\ntouched, so their next keep-both Promote re-added the retired fact and re-raised\nthe same conflict under a fresh id — a loop that member could not clear. Sync now\nreads the shared head back and mirrors each settlement into local facts using the\nsame primitives the hosted side ran, so the two cannot drift. The decision is\nderived from the head rather than a new server field: merge accept removes the\ncandidate, supersede accept flips the target to superseded pointing at the\ncandidate, and anything else reads as a reject, whose only local effect is\nclearing the conflict cross-link. Facts are mirrored before the queue entry is\ndropped, so a crash cannot lose the record of what still needs reconciling.\n\nLocal review had no hosted interlock. Settling a published proposal with `facts\nreview` left the hosted copy open, so a teammate's later apply silently overrode\nthe decision and the next sync mirrored their outcome back over it. A proposal\nrecorded in the shared ledger now refuses to settle locally and names the\n`facts proposals` command that settles it for everyone. Bulk `--apply-all` /\n`--reject-all` skips shared entries with a warning instead of failing the batch,\nwhich keeps distill's private backlog — unattributed, never shared — settleable\nin one command exactly as before.\n\nTests are mutation-verified: reverting either fix fails them. The settlement test\ndrives reconcileLocalProposalQueue directly and covers merge accept, supersede\naccept and reject, because the natural sync fixture makes the local member win\nits own proposal and therefore cannot exercise the losing side at all.\nEOF\ngit push entireio HEAD:feat/p1-canonical-signing-proposals --quiet 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"pushed: $(git log --oneline -1)\"\necho \"=== #85 now ===\"\nsleep 8\ngh pr view 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json additions,deletions,changedFiles,mergeStateStatus --jq '\"+\\(.additions)/-\\(.deletions) files=\\(.changedFiles) \\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Commit and push to PR 85"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":657884,"output_tokens":932,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":657884,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8V4WR67H8HzmM85eYZS","type":"assistant","uuid":"d574e65c-2aa1-4540-adc7-a934cb021196","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:33:20.384Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
